  "limitations": [
    "The attach routine, the probe chain and the INTERNAL_FREQ_FINE accessor execute in the sensor-hub emulator; the board lookup, SPI device find/configure, allocator, memset, GPIO services, sensor registration, SPI transfer helper, memcpy, delay and logger are supplied with authored results.",
    "Board records are decoded statically from the original registration table; that the lookup returns this record is supplied. Pin 43 and mode 4 are hub GPIO driver values; the physical pad, edge/level meaning and the SPI configuration word 0x807 are not decoded here.",
    "The GPIO interrupt is installed but left disabled; enabling, the handler 0x80f701ba, FIFO/data reads and the registered sensor callbacks are not executed. The ODR trim formula matches the LSM6DSO 26 Hz coefficient; vectors avoid values whose binary32 result depends on fused rounding.",
    "Ghidra 12.1.2 RV32 SLEIGH stores 8 bytes for c.fsw (the full 64-bit FP register, upper half zero because it does not NaN-box); the hardware stores 4. The low 4 bytes are the IEEE binary32 result, and the extra 4 bytes at 0x80f1702c are an emulator artifact recorded as such.",
    "Nothing here proves the fitted part or its electrical behaviour; this is an attach contract, not a working IMU driver."
  ],
